WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.815 --> 00:00:10.068 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Welcome to the Oceania capitals, episode one of four. First, I clear the
chosen names for a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:10.733 --> 00:00:19.986 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
We begin in the western Pacific, on three small island states: Palau, the
Caroline Islands and the Marshall Islands.

3
00:00:20.648 --> 00:00:22.947 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Ngerulmud into view.

4
00:00:26.344 --> 00:00:34.146 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Ngerulmud stands on Babeldaob, the largest island of Palau, in the western
Pacific a little north of the equator.

5
00:00:34.809 --> 00:00:46.152 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The capital only since 2006, and one of the least populous capitals in the
world, with a few thousand people; its capitol building was modelled on the
Capitol in Washington.

6
00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:53.891 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Ngerulmud as Washington's little copy on Babeldaob, a capital of a
few thousand people.

7
00:00:54.562 --> 00:00:57.975 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Palikir into view.

8
00:01:00.377 --> 00:01:07.842 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Palikir lies on the island of Pohnpei in the Caroline Islands, on a bay ringed
by the mountains of the interior.

9
00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:21.376 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The capital of Micronesia since 1989, with only a few thousand people; on the
same island stands Nan Madol, a city of stone islets built out over the water
from the twelfth century.

10
00:01:22.038 --> 00:01:28.818 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Palikir as the capital beside Nan Madol, the stone city on stilts in
the lagoon.

11
00:01:29.497 --> 00:01:31.494 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Majuro into view.

12
00:01:35.414 --> 00:01:45.352 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Majuro lies on an atoll in the Marshall Islands, in the north Pacific near the
equator, where the land is only a few metres above the sea.

13
00:01:46.018 --> 00:01:55.318 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The atoll is a ring of some sixty islets around a lagoon, and its one road
runs about fifty kilometres along that ring.

14
00:01:55.979 --> 00:02:03.781 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Majuro as a ring of sixty islets around a lagoon, with one road fifty
kilometres long.

15
00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:19.083 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Ngerulmud sits on Babeldaob, Palikir on Pohnpei, and Majuro on an atoll ring
in the Marshalls.

16
00:02:19.733 --> 00:02:30.356 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Washington's little copy on Babeldaob, the stone city of Nan Madol
beside Palikir, and the sixty islets and one long road of Majuro.
